---
const story = 'Othala at a glance, in seven steps: 1, members open an app in a browser, through the edge, Caddy, which stands in front of every app and is not part of Othala; 2, the edge proxies to an app that speaks OIDC; 3, the app redirects them to Hydra to authorize; 4, Hydra hands the login and consent challenges to the portal; 5, the portal checks their passkey session with Kratos; 6, Hydra issues the app an id_token carrying their groups; 7, for an app without OIDC, the edge first asks the portal to allow or deny the request, and proxies it only if allowed. Admins manage people on the portal\'s admin listener over the internal network, never through the edge.';
